        "text_excerpt": "TIRUVALLUR\nTIRUVANNAMALAI\nCHENGALPATTU\nVELLORE\nRANIPPETTAI\nKANCHIPURAM\nVILLUPURAM\nCHENNAI\nKANCHIPURAM\nDisaster Management Support Group (DMSG)\nNational Remote Sensing Centre, ISRO \nDept. of Space, Govt. of India\nHyderabad- 500 037\nE-Mail: flood@nrsc.gov.in\nwww.nrsc.gov.in\nnrsc\nFor Official Use\nFlood / Rain affected areas during Michaung Cyclone in Parts of TAMILNADU State\nBased on the analysis of RISAT-1A MRS SAR Satellite Image of 7-12-2023 (0600 Hrs IST)\nAbout the Event\nID:\nSatellite Observations:\nPre Flood Data\nSatellite: RISAT-1A - MRS\nDate of Pass:05-11-2023\nPost Flood Data\nSatellite: RISAT1A-MRS-SAR\nDate of Pass: 07-12-2023\nNRSC Landuse/Landcover Data\nof 2018-2019, Bhuvan Geospatial \nLegacy Data\n±\nDisclaimer : This Map  is prepared on rapid mapping mode for immediate use and sharing amongst official agencies. This provides preliminary results.\nFlood inundation may include rain water accumulation / flood water in low lying areas / paddy  fields  with standing water. No ground verification is done.\nMap extent is  limited to the available satellite coverage. All geographic information has limitations due to the scale, resolution, date and interpretation of the\noriginal source materials.                                                                             \nCitation ' NRSC (2023) - Flood Inundated areas in Part of Tamilnadu State (as on 07.12.2023)' ,  Map no :2023/CY/TN/01a/07122023, NRSC/ISRO,Hyderabad\nLocation Map\nMap\nDate of Issue: \n 2023/CY/TN/01a/07122023\n 7.12.2023\nSatellite Data Used\nReference Data Used\nHeavy rains  are witnessed during \nMichaung Cyclone (05.12.2023) and \naffected Coastal parts of Tamil Nadu \nState \n(Source: CWC, News Media)         \nThis map highlights the areas of flood\ninundation / Standing water due to\nrains just after the cyclone event\n0 20 4010\nKilometers\nDistrict Boundary\nFlood / Standing Water due to Rains\n"
